WEBVTT

00:01.140 --> 00:03.520
(November 6, AD 2095)

00:10.120 --> 00:11.220
Excuse me.

00:28.970 --> 00:31.050
I'm sorry to let you wait.

00:31.350 --> 00:33.470
Miyuki, sit down, please.

00:46.650 --> 00:48.650
I asked you to come today because

00:48.650 --> 00:50.800
I had to inform you of

00:50.800 --> 00:53.650
a series of military actions

00:54.020 --> 00:56.570
triggered by the Yokohama incident
a few days ago.

00:58.020 --> 01:00.100
The International Magic Association

01:00.100 --> 01:02.770
has concluded the explosion
that destroyed Jinhae naval port

01:02.770 --> 01:06.770
wasn't caused by a ‘radioactive weapon'.

01:08.100 --> 01:09.470
At the same time,

01:09.470 --> 01:11.170
the motion for punishment
that the government

01:11.170 --> 01:13.400
submitted to the association was rejected.

01:14.370 --> 01:17.550
I'm not aware
that there's a motion for punishment.

01:18.450 --> 01:21.650
The government seems to use this opportunity

01:21.650 --> 01:24.750
to get big concessions
from the Great Asian Union.

01:25.420 --> 01:27.770
Mr. Itsuwa Mio is

01:27.770 --> 01:30.150
with the fleet assembled in Sasebo.

01:31.300 --> 01:33.820
The use of the strategic magic 'Abyss',

01:34.300 --> 01:36.800
can Mio's body withstand it?

01:38.470 --> 01:40.870
Well, who knows that?

01:41.670 --> 01:45.150
By the way, there is
unconfirmed information.

01:45.150 --> 01:48.470
But today, we also received news
that Dr. Vesobrasov

01:48.470 --> 01:50.270
a strategic-class magician
of the New Soviet Union,

01:50.270 --> 01:53.460
has entered Vladivostok.

01:54.650 --> 01:56.670
The military chiefs of various countries,

01:56.900 --> 02:00.900
having witnessed the results
on the southern tip of the Korean Peninsula,

02:00.900 --> 02:05.270
seem to have reassessed
the effectiveness of large-scale magic.

02:10.470 --> 02:12.700
I think a joint peace with the Great Asian Union

02:12.700 --> 02:15.420
will be reached within a few days.

02:20.020 --> 02:22.100
What happened three years ago,

02:22.100 --> 02:24.370
might be finally over.

02:26.370 --> 02:28.420
That's all of our conversation.

02:28.770 --> 02:31.670
- Miyuki, you can go back.
- Eh...

02:32.700 --> 02:35.250
Tatsuya, you stay here.

02:52.790 --> 02:55.950
(The Irregular at Magic High School S3
Double Seven Arc)

04:12.000 --> 04:13.980
(April 20, AD 2096)

04:13.980 --> 04:15.100
(Student Union Office)

04:15.100 --> 04:15.980
(Student Union Office)
So, on April 24,

04:15.980 --> 04:17.570
So, on April 24,

04:17.720 --> 04:19.100
that is next Tuesday,

04:19.350 --> 04:21.500
Senator Kanda will come to visit.

04:22.020 --> 04:24.650
The purpose is to appeal to public opinion

04:24.650 --> 04:27.050
that the First High School
is in collusion with the military

04:27.320 --> 04:29.850
and that the human rights
of students are violated.

04:30.220 --> 04:32.970
Oh, isn't that very urgent?

04:33.600 --> 04:36.960
So, Shiba, how are you going to deal with it?

04:37.370 --> 04:40.300
You brought us here
because you had an idea, didn't you?

04:40.550 --> 04:41.070
Yeah...

04:50.450 --> 04:51.620
This is

04:51.850 --> 04:54.470
one of the Three Great Puzzles
of Weight Systematic Magic,

04:54.600 --> 04:57.690
Gravity Control-Type
Thermonuclear Fusion Reactor?

04:57.920 --> 04:59.920
They want to accuse the Magic High School

04:59.920 --> 05:03.450
of becoming a place of military school.

05:03.570 --> 05:06.200
If so, except for military purposes,

05:06.200 --> 05:10.420
why not show
the results of magic education?

05:12.050 --> 05:14.520
Last year, Suzune proposed

05:14.650 --> 05:17.100
the intermittent nuclear fusion reactor,

05:17.100 --> 05:19.420
whose concept is symmetrical with yours.

05:20.400 --> 05:22.870
It's not an original idea,

05:23.120 --> 05:25.170
but that's what I'm aiming for.

05:25.920 --> 05:28.500
Because the magic skills required are too high,

05:28.500 --> 05:31.150
it's still not in the practical stage.

05:31.520 --> 05:33.720
But with the strength of our students,

05:33.720 --> 05:35.450
it can be experimented for a short time.

05:36.120 --> 05:37.900
If this is achieved,

05:37.900 --> 05:39.500
no matter whether it's day or night,

05:39.500 --> 05:41.570
regardless of weather,

05:41.570 --> 05:43.600
it's possible to provide energy.

05:44.500 --> 05:46.670
It'll be the greatest demonstration

05:46.670 --> 05:49.750
of the peaceful use of magic.

05:50.170 --> 05:52.370
Okay, I'll also help.

05:52.620 --> 05:54.920
It's not just a strategy
against Senator Kanda,

05:54.920 --> 05:57.150
as someone who aspires
to be a magical technologist,

05:57.150 --> 05:59.100
I wanted to be involved.

06:03.200 --> 06:04.570
We just received permission
from the school

06:04.920 --> 06:09.070
to conduct the experiment of Gravity
Control-Type Thermonuclear Fusion Reactor.

06:09.800 --> 06:13.200
The experiment
will be supervised by Mr. Tsuzura.

06:14.320 --> 06:15.670
Then Shiba,

06:15.850 --> 06:18.970
what do you think about  the division of roles?

06:19.700 --> 06:19.900
(Gamma-ray Filter  Mitsui Honoka)

06:19.900 --> 06:21.720
(Gamma-ray Filter  Mitsui Honoka)
Please look over here.

06:21.720 --> 06:23.620
(Coulomb Force Control Isori Kei
Neutron Barrier Sakurai Minami)

06:23.620 --> 06:25.420
(Fourth Phase Shift Saegusa Izumi&Saegusa Kasumi)

06:25.420 --> 06:26.420
(Gravity Control Shiba Miyuki)

06:26.420 --> 06:29.360
(Gravity Control Shiba Miyuki)
I think they're generally the right people.

06:29.520 --> 06:33.450
I'm not impressed
with a student named Sakurai Minami.

06:33.950 --> 06:35.470
It's my cousin.

06:35.620 --> 06:35.970
(Sakurai Minami)

06:35.970 --> 06:39.600
(Sakurai Minami)
Although she's a freshman, she has a natural talent

06:39.600 --> 06:40.820
(Sakurai Minami)
for physical defensive magic.

06:40.820 --> 06:41.570
for physical defensive magic.

06:43.220 --> 06:44.420
Alright then.

06:46.120 --> 06:47.700
This system

06:47.700 --> 06:51.050
still has a lot of immature places
from a technical point of view.

06:51.670 --> 06:53.950
However, if our members can work together

06:53.950 --> 06:55.950
as a team,

06:56.320 --> 06:59.350
then the experiment,
known as one of the Three Great Puzzles,

06:59.350 --> 07:02.150
is sure to succeed.

07:02.150 --> 07:05.000
I'm sure of that.

07:11.780 --> 07:13.780
(April 23, AD 2096)

07:15.500 --> 07:17.620
Takuma, how about the high school?

07:18.150 --> 07:19.150
Are you enjoying it?

07:20.350 --> 07:23.670
Father, you're saying
something so casually!

07:23.920 --> 07:25.900
The next selection conference
of the Ten Master Clans,

07:25.900 --> 07:27.700
will be held within a year.

07:28.300 --> 07:31.100
If this goes on,
the status of the Ten Master Clans

07:31.100 --> 07:33.100
will be taken away by Saegusa
who is a fence-sitter.

07:33.100 --> 07:36.000
and we'll contend
with their underhand again!

07:36.870 --> 07:38.200
Takuma...

07:38.950 --> 07:42.300
When Saegusa advocated
the system of the Ten Master Clans,

07:42.600 --> 07:45.500
they already had the ability
to excel among the 28 Families.

07:45.670 --> 07:48.000
Isn't that the result of stealing
research achievement

07:48.000 --> 07:50.520
from the 3rd Research Institute
and the 7th Research Institute?

07:52.050 --> 07:54.350
No matter what I say, it doesn't work?

07:55.570 --> 07:58.750
That's a different story
that I ask you here today.

07:59.700 --> 08:03.800
Tomorrow, Senator Kanda of the Opposition Party
will visit the First High School.

08:04.500 --> 08:06.470
He will bring the mass communication around him.

08:06.950 --> 08:07.920
For what?

08:08.450 --> 08:11.220
He wants to do the performance
of protecting human rights

08:11.220 --> 08:13.400
of students who are forced to use magic.

08:14.120 --> 08:15.450
Human rights?

08:15.450 --> 08:16.870
What a nosy business!

08:16.870 --> 08:19.050
I know what you're trying to say,

08:19.220 --> 08:21.020
but he is a congressman.

08:21.150 --> 08:22.870
It's not good to make trouble.

08:22.870 --> 08:25.420
No matter how unpleasant they are,

08:25.570 --> 08:28.070
I won't quarrel regardless of the consequences.

08:28.250 --> 08:29.620
I'm not that naive.

08:30.570 --> 08:33.150
Even if they start a fight

08:33.500 --> 08:33.950
with you?

08:37.770 --> 08:38.770
Of course.

08:39.320 --> 08:41.550
No one wants to be so easily provoked.

08:42.400 --> 08:43.350
Is that all you want to say?

08:43.900 --> 08:46.880
Takuma, Saegusa will deal with this matter.

08:47.200 --> 08:48.250
Saegusa?

08:48.250 --> 08:50.450
Listen, mind your own business,

08:50.720 --> 08:52.670
and be responsible for what you say.

08:53.850 --> 08:56.750
We Shippou Family will not get involved in this.

08:57.500 --> 08:58.520
All right, Takuma.

08:58.900 --> 09:00.220
That's the decision.

09:01.390 --> 09:02.970
Got it!

09:05.770 --> 09:07.060
(The Irregular at Magic High School S3
Double Seven Arc Ⅲ)

09:08.900 --> 09:10.900
(April 24, AD 2096
The Stellar Reactor Experiment Day)

09:14.400 --> 09:14.900
(Citizens Party Congressman Kanda)

09:14.900 --> 09:16.280
(Citizens Party Congressman Kanda)
Mr. Kanda.

09:16.650 --> 09:18.490
(National Magic University
Affiliated First High School)
What brought you here today?

09:18.490 --> 09:20.300
(Principal Momoyama Azuma)
What brought you here today?

09:21.850 --> 09:23.270
Principal Momoyama,

09:23.400 --> 09:27.150
recently, there're unpeaceful rumors

09:27.150 --> 09:29.650
about the curriculum of Magic High School.

09:29.920 --> 09:31.750
(Vice-Principal, Yaosaka)
It's said you're brainwashing
students to become soldiers.

09:31.750 --> 09:34.120
It's said you're brainwashing
students to become soldiers.

09:34.650 --> 09:36.900
That sounds ridiculous.

09:37.250 --> 09:38.000
Right.

09:38.550 --> 09:39.820
Therefore,

09:39.820 --> 09:43.100
in order to eliminate
such an irresponsible image,

09:43.100 --> 09:46.120
I'd like to observe the classes.

09:46.920 --> 09:50.020
So many people are here suddenly,
students will be scared.

09:50.950 --> 09:53.520
I won't cause you any trouble.

10:27.220 --> 10:30.480
Vice-Principal, who are they?

10:30.800 --> 10:35.520
It's Mr. Kanda and the journalists
coming to visit our school.

10:35.950 --> 10:38.700
I hear you're doing some
extracurricular experiments.

10:38.700 --> 10:40.800
What on earth are you doing?

10:41.750 --> 10:47.000
The students are doing an experiment themselves
that is not included in the curriculum.

10:48.100 --> 10:52.700
Why do you do the experiment
that isn't regular teaching in classes?

10:53.820 --> 10:56.270
Because this experiment
is not only of academic significance,

10:56.470 --> 10:59.470
but also of high practical significance.

11:00.370 --> 11:02.500
Speaking of practical,

11:02.770 --> 11:05.870
do you mean developing a weapon

11:05.870 --> 11:08.970
like the one used in ‘Scorched Halloween'

11:08.970 --> 11:10.970
to take out enemy fleets completely?

11:11.250 --> 11:12.520
that challenges Weight Systematic Magic,
one of the Three Great Puzzles.

11:12.520 --> 11:15.970
This is a technical experiment

11:23.400 --> 11:25.050
It will start.

11:26.850 --> 11:28.250
Start the experiment.

11:35.700 --> 11:37.050
Gravity Control.

11:49.350 --> 11:51.270
Fourth Phase Shift.

11:58.550 --> 11:59.900
Neutron Barrier.

12:04.780 --> 12:06.620
Gamma-ray Filter.

12:12.070 --> 12:13.290
Gravity Control.

12:35.720 --> 12:37.270
Coulomb Force Control.

13:09.050 --> 13:10.700
The experiment is over.

13:16.470 --> 13:18.500
Dispel Gamma-ray Filter.

13:19.300 --> 13:20.620
Dispel Gravity Control.

13:23.970 --> 13:25.800
Keep Neutron Barrier like that.

13:39.070 --> 13:40.550
Here is the result of the analysis.

13:40.970 --> 13:44.170
The gas components are water vapor, hydrogen,

13:44.170 --> 13:46.950
deuterium and helium.

13:46.950 --> 13:49.820
No mixing of radioactive materials is observed!

13:51.600 --> 13:53.600
Please start filling the water.

14:00.850 --> 14:02.500
Dispel Neutron Barrier.

14:24.770 --> 14:25.450
Woa...Ah... Eh...

14:35.500 --> 14:39.200
With Resident Gravity Control-Type
Magic as the core technology,

14:39.320 --> 14:41.570
continuous thermonuclear fusion experiment

14:41.570 --> 14:44.120
achieved the desired goal.

14:45.650 --> 14:47.850
The ‘Stellar Reactor' experiment is a success.

14:53.780 --> 14:55.780
Congrats!

15:01.970 --> 15:03.020
Excuse me!

15:04.570 --> 15:06.770
What the hell was that?

15:07.900 --> 15:12.300
It's an experiment on a resident Gravity
Control-Type Thermonuclear Fusion Reactor.

15:13.700 --> 15:17.800
Should the practical use
of nuclear fusion reactor be given up?

15:17.950 --> 15:20.230
We can't give up.

15:20.650 --> 15:24.200
Research itself continues in various fields,

15:24.320 --> 15:27.570
and nuclear fusion research
using magic is part of that.

15:28.370 --> 15:29.950
Is the goal of nuclear fusion research

15:29.950 --> 15:33.620
to achieve nuclear fusion explosions
through magic?

15:33.950 --> 15:37.520
For example, the one used
in 'Scorched Halloween'?

15:40.200 --> 15:43.080
Excuse me, but what were you looking at?

15:43.080 --> 15:43.600
Ah.

15:44.450 --> 15:46.700
If it is only to cause a small explosion,

15:46.700 --> 15:49.950
there is no need to create
such a precise technique.

15:50.450 --> 15:53.300
If it is to cause a large explosion as you said,

15:53.300 --> 15:56.150
there's no need to use such a technique.

15:57.050 --> 15:58.650
Today's experiment

15:58.650 --> 16:02.250
is a nuclear fusion experiment
as an energy source for society's infrastructure.

16:03.200 --> 16:05.200
If the "Stellar Reactor"
is put into practical use,

16:05.300 --> 16:10.400
mankind will be able to use
more abundant energy than today.

16:12.250 --> 16:14.780
What do you think, Mr. Kanda?

16:15.250 --> 16:19.620
It's the peaceful social
contribution spirit of our students.

16:20.050 --> 16:21.770
I... I see.

16:23.220 --> 16:26.550
I think the attitude of contributing to

16:26.550 --> 16:28.970
to the prosperity of society is remarkable.

16:34.700 --> 16:37.600
I saw a valuable experiment.

16:38.700 --> 16:40.950
Then I'll be leaving.

16:48.920 --> 16:52.150
Mr. Tsuzura, is it exaggerated?

16:52.720 --> 16:54.770
Well, it's embarrassing.

16:54.900 --> 16:57.020
I was too angry

16:57.020 --> 17:00.290
because my students' spirits
had been deliberately distorted.

17:00.670 --> 17:03.220
The spirit?

17:04.820 --> 17:09.100
The experiment is still very immature
from a technical point of view.

17:09.870 --> 17:13.600
But I think his fighting spirit

17:13.770 --> 17:15.800
of wanting to change the shape
of society through magic

17:15.970 --> 17:20.750
is valuable,
regardless of technical completion.

17:23.120 --> 17:26.850
I think that the spirit to change

17:26.850 --> 17:28.150
what they mean to society

17:28.150 --> 17:31.650
is very valuable.

17:36.070 --> 17:38.000
Surprise!

17:38.000 --> 17:40.330
Happy birthday, Tatsuya!

17:40.330 --> 17:42.450
Is Miyuki doing well too?

17:43.120 --> 17:44.150
Shocked?

17:44.520 --> 17:47.300
Even the most capable Tatsuya,
you didn't imagine

17:47.300 --> 17:49.820
that I'd send a birthday video letter, right?

17:50.100 --> 17:53.420
Ah, but if you think
I can't celebrate a birthday,

17:53.420 --> 17:56.250
I'll be lonely, too...

17:56.350 --> 17:57.050
Ah...

17:57.650 --> 17:59.570
Well, Just forget I said that!

17:59.770 --> 18:01.350
I don't feel lonely.

18:01.720 --> 18:04.470
I'm not really lonely!

18:04.470 --> 18:07.770
Don't get me wrong!
Absolutely no! Tatsuya...

18:08.850 --> 18:09.800
It's Miyuki.

18:10.420 --> 18:12.650
Brother, are you available?

18:13.370 --> 18:15.050
Yeah, I'm going there now.

18:31.450 --> 18:34.270
Brother, just a little moment,

18:34.270 --> 18:37.900
can I celebrate your birthday alone?

18:40.220 --> 18:42.100
Well, brother?

18:42.370 --> 18:43.920
Ah. Thank you.

18:50.950 --> 18:53.570
Happy birthday, brother.

18:54.370 --> 18:56.820
Brother,  thank you for being here

18:57.100 --> 18:58.350
with me.

18:59.170 --> 19:00.250
Thank you.

19:00.820 --> 19:03.350
I'm grateful to be your brother.

19:13.340 --> 19:16.380
(Magic High School Students
The Stellar Reactor Experiment Success)

19:18.150 --> 19:19.400
It seems that Tatsuya

19:19.400 --> 19:22.170
has achieved great results.

19:24.000 --> 19:24.750
Right.

19:29.640 --> 19:30.960
(November 6, AD 2095)

19:31.070 --> 19:34.350
It's been three years since I saw you
like this face to face.

19:35.100 --> 19:37.420
This is the first time

19:37.420 --> 19:38.900
I've heard you say that, aunt.

19:39.700 --> 19:41.450
Is that so?

19:41.450 --> 19:44.800
Yes. So, what are you going to say?

19:45.700 --> 19:49.100
You made a big move this time, Tatsuya.

19:49.600 --> 19:51.400
No, I'm flattered.

19:52.020 --> 19:57.520
But for Yotsuba,
this is a very difficult thing for him.

19:57.520 --> 20:00.600
Did any inconvenience occur?

20:02.370 --> 20:04.520
The Stars is going into action.

20:05.220 --> 20:06.650
America?

20:08.520 --> 20:10.170
They've identified

20:10.170 --> 20:13.050
that the explosion that destroyed the fleet
of the Great Asian Union,

20:13.050 --> 20:16.200
in which the suspects

20:16.700 --> 20:18.920
are pointed to you and Miyuki.

20:19.720 --> 20:22.720
If America would think its hegemony to be shaken,

20:22.720 --> 20:26.450
it may depend on
its own strength to eliminate.

20:27.170 --> 20:30.450
If there is a possibility
that it will affect Yotsuba,

20:30.450 --> 20:32.920
they will send another assassin.

20:33.070 --> 20:34.460
That's what you mean, right?

20:35.000 --> 20:36.000
I will bear it in mind.

20:42.770 --> 20:45.650
Tatsuya, leave school.

20:50.520 --> 20:53.230
What do you want me to do
after I leave school?

20:53.550 --> 20:56.020
Stay here to do self-reflection for a while.

20:56.300 --> 21:00.050
I'll send someone else to be Miyuki's guardian.

21:02.050 --> 21:03.450
I refuse.

21:05.450 --> 21:08.100
You don't obey my orders?

21:08.570 --> 21:10.270
The one who can give me orders

21:10.570 --> 21:12.120
is only Miyuki.

21:33.970 --> 21:37.220
It seems that you're clearly lenient to me.

21:38.300 --> 21:39.970
Of course, okay?

21:39.970 --> 21:43.250
Because you're my lovely nephew.

21:44.020 --> 21:47.100
Well, excluding that, you did pretty well.

21:47.370 --> 21:51.800
So this time, I will fulfill your willfulness.

21:53.220 --> 21:54.720
Thank you very much.

21:55.050 --> 21:58.770
It's okay. Because it's a small reward

21:58.950 --> 22:01.220
for breaking my magic.

22:04.270 --> 22:09.050
I wonder if it's worth
listening to his selfish wishes.

23:36.230 --> 23:38.620
(The Irregular at Magic High School S3
Double Seven Arc Ⅳ)
